# Models and training

`PDMNet`: `[B, history, F] →` unidirectional GRU|LSTM → last hidden → head. No other architectures.

**Bearings head `rul`:** Softplus → non-negative RUL (normalized). Loss `SmoothL1Loss`. Best epoch = unit-equal val MAE. Metrics in physical seconds.

**Filters head `weibull`:** `lambda>0`, `k>0`. Right-censored NLL in `losses.weibull_nll`. Point forecast = Weibull **median** remaining life (`weibull_median_rul`). Do not MSE on planned-replacement time. Best epoch = unit-equal val NLL. Val MAE only on observed events, with their count.

```text
r = duration_s / time_scale_s
loss = -event * log_f(r) - (1-event) * log_S(r)
```

`time_scale_s` from train only. Keep NLL numerically stable (clamp, no NaN/Inf).

**Training**
- `device=auto`: CUDA → MPS → CPU; log fallback reason
- Sample units then windows (long runs must not dominate)
- Save `best.pt` + `last.pt`, config, split, versions. Smoke runs: `Smoke test — not a quality benchmark`
- Resume only from `last` when dataset, split, features, scaler, architecture match
- Infer with `model.eval()` + `no_grad`; reload must match within numeric tolerance
- Do not mix dataset checkpoints

**Baselines (keep even if NN loses):** bearings `Age-only` (train-regime median duration − age); filters linear Δp trend to 600 Pa, else `No finite trend estimate` — never a fake huge RUL.
